<title>USA: Bristol-Myers gets Japanes okay on Taxol.</title>
<headline>Bristol-Myers gets Japanes okay on Taxol.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bristol-Myers Squibb Co said Thursday it had received authorization from the Japanese Ministry of Health and Welfare to market Taxol for the treatment of advanced ovarian cancer.</p>
<p>Taxol is currently marketed in 74 countries for the treatment of advanced ovarian cancer and metastatic breast cancer.</p>
<p>Bristol-Myers said it has filed supplemental applications to extend the Japanese approval so that Taxol can also be made available in Japan for the treatment of breast and non-small-cell lung cancers.</p>
</text>
